# CRR Use Case — Artifact Inventory (Sentinel shared capability platform)
 
Working inventory of artifacts Steve is creating/gathering for the Credit Risk Review (CRR) tenant. Tracked in Steve's internal spreadsheet (crr_artifact_inventory.xlsx, delivered 2026-08-20). Items marked ✦ were on Steve's initial list.
 
## Process & Training
- ✦ **CRR end-user process walkthrough** — Step-by-step guide showing how a CRR analyst uses the platform end-to-end: initiating a workpaper, reviewing and editing drafts, finalizing and routing for review. (Primary near-term deliverable.)
- **Quick reference guides / FAQ** — One-page job aids distilled from the walkthrough for day-to-day use after training.
## Content & Grounding
- ✦ **Workpaper type inventory & content ownership matrix** — Catalog of every CRR workpaper type, by section, with owning team/role for each content area.
- ✦ **House style writing guide** — Voice, tone, terminology, and formatting conventions all drafts must follow.
- ✦ **Policy reference corpus & mapping** — At minimum, which policies apply to which workpaper types; ideally the full versioned corpus.
- **Policy corpus operating model** — Who refreshes the corpus, on what cadence, with version and effective-date control.
- **Gold-standard exemplar workpapers** — Sanitized examples of excellent completed workpapers per type; grounding material and QA benchmark.
- **Canonical annotated templates** — Official template per type, annotated by section: system-drafted vs. analyst judgment vs. data-fed.
- **Source data inventory** — Systems/documents feeding each workpaper section (loan system, spreads, appraisals, credit agreements) and how each is accessed.
- **Glossary & definitions** — Risk rating definitions, regulatory classifications, house acronyms.
## Quality & Acceptance
- ✦ **Workpaper review standards** — Standards completed workpapers are reviewed against.
- **Definition of done / acceptance criteria** — Per workpaper type, what a platform draft must meet before an analyst works from it.
- **Evaluation rubric & error severity taxonomy** — Scoring framework for output quality, with error classes ranked by severity.
- **Golden test set** — Sanitized real cases with known-correct outcomes for UAT and regression checking.
- **UAT plan & test scripts** — Test scenarios for the CRR use case, derived from the process walkthrough.
## Governance & Compliance
- **AI / model risk use-case documentation** — Use-case risk assessment, human-in-the-loop control description, reviewer attestation requirements.
- **Records retention & audit trail requirements** — How platform-produced workpapers are retained and what audit trail must exist.
- **Regulatory guidance mapping** — Mapping to the Interagency Guidance on Credit Risk Review Systems (independence and coverage preserved).
## Adoption & Operating Model
- **Baseline metrics capture** — Pre-launch time-per-workpaper and rework/re-review rates, to demonstrate impact later.
- **Pilot group & feedback loop** — Named pilot users plus a triage process for routing bad outputs to fixes.
- **Shared-vs-tenant asset decision log** — Which assets are platform-wide vs. CRR-owned, coordinated with the other two tenants.
- **BRD requirements traceability matrix** — CRR requirements mapped to BRD coverage so gaps surface before UAT.
- **Artifact ownership & refresh cadence** — Named owner and update cycle for every artifact in this inventory.
